Independent boot-test suite for golden guest images (kind `image-first-boot` of ou-test-attest).

  image-boot-suite <image.qcow2>     exit 0 = every check passed AND every stage ran, 1 = a check failed, other = infrastructure error (no attestation)
  staticchecks.py                    offline hardening checks over an extracted image tree
  icssim.py                          throw-away ICS callback simulator (protocol pinned to ics.guest.callback by ics/tests/test_golden_prod.py)
  tcprelay.py                        qemu guestfwd helper (the guest can reach exactly the simulator, nothing else)
  install-testsuite.sh               root-owned install into the boot-test machine

Attestor contract (fixes-r7 `ou-test-attest run image-first-boot <path>` -> <lib>/image-first-boot <private copy>, attestation v2, exit 0/1/other):
  oci-signing's testrunner/image-first-boot -> sudo image-boot-root -> boots the copy in the boot-test machine. That helper must run THIS suite there
  (see docs/status/golden-image-prod-results.md "Integration with the attestor" for the exact change) and derive the verdict from the exit status and the
  final `SUMMARY ... failed=0 ... complete=True` line, which this program prints itself.
Needs in the machine: qemu-system-x86_64, qemu-img, openssl, e2fsprogs (debugfs), util-linux (sfdisk), python3 with `cryptography`, ~6 GiB free in
OU_TEST_WORK (default /var/tmp), 1.2 GiB RAM. Wall clock under TCG: see the results document. The guest is untrusted code under emulation: the user-mode
network is `restrict=on`; run it inside the throw-away boot-test machine, never on the signer host.
